luru. Founded 1909.", "newValue": "The Indian Institute of Science (IISc), established in 1909 in Bengaluru, India, stands as a beacon of scientific research and education in South Asia. Founded through the vision of J.R.D. Tata and supported by the government of Mysore, IISc represents a pivotal milestone in India's journey toward scientific modernity. Its establishment coincided with a period of burgeoning nationalism and the quest for self-reliance in science and technology, marking a significant departure from colonial dependence on foreign expertise.

